@meta
id: 13-06
title: Drill — the negative row
chapter: 13
type: drill
skills: regex-classes
par: 14
minutes: 4
reps: 8
vscode: scan the amount column by eye, click the row, Ctrl+Shift+K
open: settlement.csv

@brief
Eight times: one row in this settlement file has a negative amount, and
the importer rejects the whole file because of it. Delete that row.

The dash in the `notes` column marks an empty note, so searching for a
dash is not enough, and the SKUs have a dash followed by digits. A
comma, a dash, a digit — that is the shape of a negative amount and
nothing else in the file.

@keys
| `\d` | a digit |
| `dd` | delete the line |

@hints
The amount is a field, so it has a comma in front of it. Put the comma
in the pattern.
--
`/,-\d` `Enter` and `dd`.

@solution
/,-\d<Enter>  dd  :wq<Enter>

Twelve keystrokes. The pattern is three characters and each of them is
carrying weight: the comma rules out the SKUs, the dash rules out the
positive amounts, the `\d` rules out the empty notes.

By rep eight the class should be arriving in your fingers as one unit —
`\d` is a key, not a backslash and then a letter. The same goes for
`\w` and `\s` once you have used them a few times.

@start settlement.csv
order_id,customer_id,sku,amount,notes,status
ord_9101,cus_4471,SKU-2231,1499,-,PAID
ord_9104,cus_1180,SKU-0917,2599,-,PAID
ord_9112,cus_4471,SKU-2231,1499,replacement,PAID
ord_9118,cus_3302,SKU-1540,4200,-,PAID
ord_9120,cus_2210,SKU-0917,-2599,customer-return,PAID
ord_9125,cus_7754,SKU-3300,15990,-,PENDING
ord_9127,cus_1180,SKU-1540,2199,-,PAID
ord_9131,cus_9021,SKU-2231,1499,gift-wrap,PAID

@expected settlement.csv
order_id,customer_id,sku,amount,notes,status
ord_9101,cus_4471,SKU-2231,1499,-,PAID
ord_9104,cus_1180,SKU-0917,2599,-,PAID
